# Line endings are not cosmetic in this repository.
#
# Almost everything here is a shell script that runs on Linux or inside a
# container. Git for Windows checks files out as CRLF by default, and a shell
# script with CRLF endings fails as:
#
#     /bin/sh^M: bad interpreter: No such file or directory
#
# which tells the reader nothing useful. Worse, `.env` files and the Docker
# entrypoints would carry stray carriage returns into container environments,
# where they turn a password into "secret\r" and the database refuses the login.
#
# So: normalise to LF on commit AND on checkout, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The port patch must survive byte for byte -- `patch` counts characters, and a
# rewritten line ending makes every hunk fail to apply.
*.patch -text

# Binary, never transform.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
*.gz  binary

# Wiki pack inputs preserve the donor's bytes, including .sub descriptor EOLs.
/linux-port-mt2009/client-patch-wiki/** -text
# Said's Turkish helper and COOP guide ship in the client package as he wrote
# them (CRLF; cmd.exe reads the .bat), not normalised to LF.
/linux-port-mt2009/client-coop/Turkce-Yap.bat -text
/linux-port-mt2009/client-coop/COOP*arkadasinla*.txt -text

# Translation tables whose trailing spaces and tabs are text: a label a value
# is appended to ("Full skip: "), the locale's empty third column. git's
# whitespace check would have them taken away (Said's Turkish, 20 October).
/linux-port-mt2009/client-locale/locale/** -whitespace
/data/playerbot_quest_texts_*.tsv -whitespace
# A stock root module rendered whole for a donor keeps its bytes, trailing
# tabs included, so the renderer's replay over the published root stays exact
# (uiquest.py for Kiciamol's quest curtain, #59).
/linux-port-mt2009/client-root/uiquest.py -whitespace

# The published client's gamedata pack the panel builds the client's item and
# monster tables over (files/client_protos.py): its bytes are compared by SHA-256.
/files/client_base/gamedata.* binary
# Colide's native Auto Lowy sources stay his bytes (some generated files are
# CRLF); clientify copies them into the client tree unchanged.
/linux-port-mt2009/port/client/UserInterface/autohunt/** -text
